# Musical consonance and the small-integer frequency ratios. Two tones sound consonant when their frequencies stand in a
# simple whole-number ratio, because their overtones line up and the beating that Plomp and Levelt measured as roughness
# falls away. The octave is two to one, the perfect fifth three to two, the perfect fourth four to three, the major third
# five to four, the minor third six to five, each a ratio of small integers. The intervals compose by multiplying ratios:
# a fifth stacked on a fourth is an octave, three-halves times four-thirds is two, and a major third stacked on a minor
# third is a fifth, five-fourths times six-fifths is three-halves. But the small ratios do not close on themselves, and
# that gap is why tuning is hard. Twelve perfect fifths overshoot seven octaves by the Pythagorean comma, three to the
# twelfth above two to the nineteenth, and four just fifths overshoot two octaves and a major third by the syntonic comma,
# eighty-one to eighty. This file checks the interval compositions and both commas by exact integer arithmetic, tying the
# phonology of consonant sound to number.

# A fifth stacked on a fourth is an octave: (3/2) * (4/3) = 2, checked by cross-multiplication 3 * 4 = 2 * (2 * 3) = 12.
hold fifth-on-fourth-is-an-octave
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      code 3
      code 4
    call multiply
      code 2
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 3

# A major third stacked on a minor third is a fifth: (5/4) * (6/5) = 3/2, checked as (5*6)*2 = 3*(4*5), both sixty.
hold major-third-on-minor-third-is-a-fifth
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      call multiply
        code 5
        code 6
      code 2
    call multiply
      code 3
      call multiply
        code 4
        code 5

# The Pythagorean comma: twelve fifths, 3^12 = 729 * 729 = 531441, overshoot seven octaves, 2^19 = 512 * 1024 = 524288.
hold pythagorean-comma-numerator-is-three-to-the-twelfth
  call is-equal
    code 531441
    call multiply
      code 729
      code 729

hold pythagorean-comma-denominator-is-two-to-the-nineteenth
  call is-equal
    code 524288
    call multiply
      code 512
      code 1024

# Twelve fifths land above seven octaves, so the comma is a real gap: 531441 above 524288.
hold twelve-fifths-overshoot-seven-octaves
  call is-above
    call multiply
      code 729
      code 729
    call multiply
      code 512
      code 1024

# The syntonic comma is 81 to 80: 3^4 = 9 * 9 = 81 above 16 * 5 = 80, the gap between four just fifths and a just major
# third two octaves up.
hold syntonic-comma-is-eighty-one-to-eighty
  call is-above
    call multiply
      code 9
      code 9
    call multiply
      code 16
      code 5
